WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.805 --> 00:00:06.725
Back up! Move, move, move!

2
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.064
- Not that I'm worried, but...

3
00:00:12.064 --> 00:00:14.483
...what if The Chameleon knows
we're coming?

4
00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:16.693
Why, she could be anywhere, anyone.

5
00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:19.571
Li, would you please show
a little backbone?

6
00:00:19.571 --> 00:00:23.075
I'm sorry, but bravery was never
really my specialty.

7
00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:27.871
You don't have to be brave.
You just have to act brave.

8
00:00:27.871 --> 00:00:30.040
Act brave? Got it.

9
00:00:30.707 --> 00:00:32.709
- Ah!
- Oh!

10
00:00:32.709 --> 00:00:34.127
Oh, Li!

11
00:00:34.127 --> 00:00:36.505
- Hold on!

12
00:00:36.505 --> 00:00:39.341
Hold me, Ping! It's all been for nothing!

13
00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:40.843
Please, no.

14
00:00:40.843 --> 00:00:43.262
- I'm too young!

15
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:48.559
How was that for acting brave?

16
00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:50.477
Keep working on it.

17
00:00:54.523 --> 00:00:56.733
Juniper City.

18
00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:58.652
It's going to be great
to be back home again.

19
00:00:58.652 --> 00:01:00.654
Does your family live there too?

20
00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:02.990
They would. If I had a family.

21
00:01:03.657 --> 00:01:06.160
It wasn't easy being a little fox
in a big city.

22
00:01:07.077 --> 00:01:09.329
So I had to survive any way I could.

23
00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:10.372
Hey!

24
00:01:10.372 --> 00:01:13.500
Grifting. Shilling. Gaffing.

25
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.128
Stop running! Stop running!

26
00:01:21.842 --> 00:01:24.219
Whoa, you're an orphan? So am I.

27
00:01:24.219 --> 00:01:25.679
Well, I mean I was.

28
00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:29.600
My goose dad adopted me,
and then later, my panda dad found me.

29
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.312
Goose dads, panda dads.
Guess it takes all kinds.

30
00:01:33.312 --> 00:01:34.855
- Right, Mom?

31
00:01:35.606 --> 00:01:37.733
Then, one day, a local took me in.

32
00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:41.195
Put a roof over my head,
gave me clothes to wear, food to eat.

33
00:01:41.195 --> 00:01:43.572
After that, I was never alone again.

34
00:01:43.572 --> 00:01:44.781
I guess we both got lucky.

35
00:01:44.781 --> 00:01:45.824
I guess.

36
00:01:45.824 --> 00:01:48.202
Hey, tell me something.
Back in the Valley of Geese...

37
00:01:48.202 --> 00:01:49.244
Peace.

38
00:01:49.244 --> 00:01:50.746
...what did that angry little squirrel
mean...

39
00:01:50.746 --> 00:01:51.663
Red panda.

40
00:01:51.663 --> 00:01:53.707
...when he said you had to
find your successor?

41
00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:57.294
Now that I'm supposed to become
Spiritual Leader,

42
00:01:57.294 --> 00:02:00.380
I have to find a worthy successor
to take over as the Dragon Warrior.

43
00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.549
Once you're on top,
that's where you wanna stay, right?

44
00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:05.636
No, it's just that-- What do I know
about being a Spiritual Leader?

45
00:02:05.636 --> 00:02:08.180
I can't even come up with
one of those cool-sounding proverbs.

46
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.849
"Life's greatest enemy is"...

47
00:02:10.849 --> 00:02:13.060
Uh, I don't know. Stairs?

48
00:02:13.644 --> 00:02:14.770
Okay.

49
00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.147
Everyone knows
life's greatest enemy is time.

50
00:02:18.106 --> 00:02:21.193
I guess it's just easier to hold on
to the life you know

51
00:02:21.193 --> 00:02:22.694
than move on to the one you don't.

52
00:02:22.694 --> 00:02:24.488
Hey, that was pretty good.

53
00:02:24.488 --> 00:02:25.405
Yeah.

54
00:02:25.405 --> 00:02:29.243
Maybe she should be the Spiritual Leader
of the Valley of Geese.

55
00:02:31.161 --> 00:02:33.205
Whoa, that guy.
He drinks like a fish.

56
00:02:33.205 --> 00:02:34.748
Should he be driving?

57
00:02:59.773 --> 00:03:02.901
We've come to pay tribute,
as you requested.

58
00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.778
Looks a little light.

59
00:03:04.778 --> 00:03:06.655
Go back out and get me more!

60
00:03:06.655 --> 00:03:07.573
More?

61
00:03:07.573 --> 00:03:08.740
But-- But, Chameleon--

62
00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.369
Go! Before I toss you
down another flight of stairs.

63
00:03:15.205 --> 00:03:18.500
At last, my destiny approaches.

64
00:03:22.212 --> 00:03:27.717
I'll expand my rule from Juniper City
to every city and town and village

65
00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:31.346
from here to the Valley of Peace
and beyond!

66
00:03:35.726 --> 00:03:40.646
They will all know the name
of The Chameleon!

67
00:03:40.646 --> 00:03:41.982
Wake up! Wake up! Wake up!

68
00:03:41.982 --> 00:03:46.195
Ah! Zhen! I had a vision.
I saw The Chameleon.

69
00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:49.239
She's gonna take over cities and towns
and the Valley of Peace.

70
00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:50.949
A vision?

71
00:03:50.949 --> 00:03:52.492
While you were asleep?

72
00:03:52.492 --> 00:03:53.911
I'm pretty sure that's just a dream.

73
00:03:53.911 --> 00:03:55.704
Not a dream, a vision.

74
00:03:55.704 --> 00:03:57.789
Either I had a bad dumpling
before I went to sleep,

75
00:03:57.789 --> 00:03:59.625
or it's a Dragon Warrior thing.

76
00:03:59.625 --> 00:04:01.627
We got to get to The Chameleon
and take her down.

77
00:04:01.627 --> 00:04:03.587
Well, then you're in luck.

78
00:04:03.587 --> 00:04:05.756
Welcome to Juniper City.

79
00:04:10.969 --> 00:04:12.387
Whoa!

80
00:04:14.848 --> 00:04:17.684
This is the place where you can be
whatever you wanna be,

81
00:04:17.684 --> 00:04:19.978
do whatever you wanna do,

82
00:04:19.978 --> 00:04:23.273
and steal whatever you wanna steal.

83
00:04:23.273 --> 00:04:24.358
Uh, if that's your thing.

84
00:04:24.358 --> 00:04:27.986
Land ho!

85
00:04:29.238 --> 00:04:31.198
Whoa. That came out of nowhere.

86
00:04:41.625 --> 00:04:42.501
Ah!

87
00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:44.878
- Whoa!
- Move!

88
00:04:44.878 --> 00:04:46.630
- Look out!
- Sorry!

89
00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.714
Out of the way!

90
00:04:48.549 --> 00:04:50.509
I've never seen so much traffic before.

91
00:04:50.509 --> 00:04:52.594
You don't have rush hour
in the Valley of Peace?

92
00:04:52.594 --> 00:04:54.888
No one's ever in that much of a rush. Oof.

93
00:04:56.557 --> 00:04:57.933
Come on!

94
00:05:02.563 --> 00:05:04.481
Well, sure is good to be home again.

95
00:05:04.481 --> 00:05:06.316
The sights. The sounds.

96
00:05:06.316 --> 00:05:09.027
The smells.

97
00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.869
It's a wonton wonderland!

98
00:05:18.996 --> 00:05:20.038
Yeah!

99
00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:24.960
- Po. Po!

100
00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.461
Focus!

101
00:05:26.461 --> 00:05:28.547
This city is the most amazing place
I've ever seen!

102
00:05:28.547 --> 00:05:31.925
I used to feel the same way
until The Chameleon got her claws into it.

103
00:05:43.187 --> 00:05:45.314
Tonight, we take down The Chameleon.

104
00:05:45.314 --> 00:05:46.440
Oh, yeah.

105
00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.110
I'll show you where this villainous
sorceress lurks as she dominates the city.

106
00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:53.155
Is she lurking in that villainous tower
dominating the city?

107
00:05:54.948 --> 00:05:55.949
How'd you know?

108
00:05:55.949 --> 00:05:57.951
Eh, not my first time
taking down a villain.

109
00:05:57.951 --> 00:05:59.036
Let's keep moving.

110
00:05:59.036 --> 00:06:00.454
- Hey, Zhen!
- Heya, Zhen.

111
00:06:00.454 --> 00:06:01.622
Long time no see.

112
00:06:01.622 --> 00:06:02.539
How you doing, Zhen?

113
00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:04.791
Wow, you're quite the local celeb.

114
00:06:04.791 --> 00:06:08.045
Yeah, well, let's just say
a face like mine is hard to forget.

115
00:06:10.756 --> 00:06:12.883
What? You're a wanted criminal?

116
00:06:12.883 --> 00:06:16.470
You sound surprised. Is this surprising?
I don't think this is surprising.

117
00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.472
You never mentioned
you were wanted.

118
00:06:18.472 --> 00:06:19.806
Don't worry.

119
00:06:19.806 --> 00:06:22.017
The law has better things to do
than look for me.

120
00:06:22.017 --> 00:06:24.645
- Hey, fox.
- We've been looking for you.

121
00:06:24.645 --> 00:06:25.771
Must be a slow workweek.

122
00:06:25.771 --> 00:06:27.022
I'll handle this.

123
00:06:27.022 --> 00:06:30.192
Morning, officers.
Dragon Warrior here.

124
00:06:30.192 --> 00:06:33.654
The fox and I are here
on official Dragon Warrior biz.

125
00:06:33.654 --> 00:06:35.280
- Dragon who?
- Warrior what?

126
00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.740
Dragon Warrior.

127
00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.034
Anyone? Nothing?

128
00:06:39.034 --> 00:06:41.036
Perhaps you know me better as...

129
00:06:41.703 --> 00:06:44.164
the Kung Fu Panda!

130
00:06:45.332 --> 00:06:47.209
- Wait, wait!

131
00:06:47.209 --> 00:06:49.086
Can you believe that guy?

132
00:06:49.086 --> 00:06:50.254
Aw, come on!

133
00:06:50.254 --> 00:06:53.549
Okay, so we tried it your way.
Now we try it mine.

134
00:06:55.175 --> 00:06:59.972
- Wait, what's your way--

135
00:06:59.972 --> 00:07:01.056
Sorry.

136
00:07:02.432 --> 00:07:04.142
Come on, come on, come on, come on!

137
00:07:04.768 --> 00:07:07.354
You can't run away from the law.
You're a wanted criminal!

138
00:07:07.354 --> 00:07:10.065
Yeah? Well, it looks like
I'm not the only one.

139
00:07:10.065 --> 00:07:12.359
Wow. City life really is fast-paced.

140
00:07:12.359 --> 00:07:14.319
We gotta get out of here
before they call for...

141
00:07:16.572 --> 00:07:17.865
...backup.

142
00:07:22.619 --> 00:07:24.037
That's a lot of bull.

143
00:07:24.037 --> 00:07:25.581
- Run!

144
00:07:32.296 --> 00:07:34.173
- Let's go, let's go!
- Oh!

145
00:07:43.223 --> 00:07:44.516
Ow!

146
00:08:12.127 --> 00:08:13.128
Let's go.

147
00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.840
Whoa! Whoa!

148
00:08:19.384 --> 00:08:21.053
I'm falling...

149
00:08:21.053 --> 00:08:22.888
very slowly.

150
00:08:24.598 --> 00:08:26.975
Ow!

151
00:08:38.403 --> 00:08:39.655
Sorry.

152
00:08:56.004 --> 00:08:56.964
Whew.

153
00:09:04.429 --> 00:09:05.430
There they are!

154
00:09:07.266 --> 00:09:09.518
We don't have time for a drum solo!

155
00:09:11.144 --> 00:09:12.563
We're trapped.

156
00:09:24.908 --> 00:09:25.993
It isn't much farther now.

157
00:09:25.993 --> 00:09:28.662
You always say that,
and it's always so much farther.

158
00:09:30.956 --> 00:09:33.792
Whoa. What is this place?

159
00:09:33.792 --> 00:09:35.252
Home sweet home.

160
00:09:35.252 --> 00:09:38.839
Some of the best crooks and criminals
in all of Juniper City live here.

161
00:09:40.966 --> 00:09:44.386
Careful. These guys will steal your pants
right off ya, and you'll never know it.

162
00:09:47.764 --> 00:09:49.099
Uh-oh.

163
00:09:49.099 --> 00:09:51.351
Now, you kids be careful
with those fireworks.

164
00:09:55.981 --> 00:09:57.065
Ooh!

165
00:10:02.362 --> 00:10:03.488
Ow!

166
00:10:07.868 --> 00:10:10.787
Oh!

167
00:10:10.787 --> 00:10:13.040
So you're friends
with all these people?

168
00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.333
They're practically family.

169
00:10:14.333 --> 00:10:15.667
Zhen!

170
00:10:20.797 --> 00:10:23.008
Oh! Is that really you?

171
00:10:23.008 --> 00:10:25.469
Han, my old mentor.

172
00:10:25.469 --> 00:10:28.430
I always knew someday you'll find your way
home back to the den.

173
00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:29.890
And when you did...

174
00:10:31.475 --> 00:10:34.520
...I'd be sure to give you
a proper homecoming.

175
00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:35.854
Family, huh?

176
00:10:35.854 --> 00:10:37.189
More like distant cousins.

177
00:10:37.189 --> 00:10:39.107
All right. How should we do this?

178
00:10:39.107 --> 00:10:42.277
Quick and painless?
Or slow and painful?

179
00:10:42.277 --> 00:10:45.697
Slow and painful.
Slow and painful.

180
00:10:45.697 --> 00:10:48.450
All right, you little scamps.
Slow and painful it is.

181
00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:49.993
- Hooray!
- Yay!

182
00:10:49.993 --> 00:10:51.578
You really don't wanna do this.

183
00:10:51.578 --> 00:10:52.663
And why is that?

184
00:10:52.663 --> 00:10:54.915
Because if you so much as
lay one claw on me,

185
00:10:54.915 --> 00:10:56.583
you're gonna have to answer to...

186
00:10:57.292 --> 00:10:59.294
the Dragon Warrior.

187
00:10:59.294 --> 00:11:01.922
Warrior, warrior, warrior,
warrior, warrior.

188
00:11:03.215 --> 00:11:04.216
Who?

189
00:11:06.635 --> 00:11:09.930
Oh, man. Are my adventures
really that regional?

190
00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.348
Introduce them, Po,

191
00:11:12.266 --> 00:11:14.434
to your fists.

192
00:11:19.481 --> 00:11:23.694
Remember, Po, there are other ways
to bring peace than by kicking butt.

193
00:11:23.694 --> 00:11:25.696
Ah, come on. Really? Now?

194
00:11:25.696 --> 00:11:27.573
Yes, now.

195
00:11:27.573 --> 00:11:30.909
Hold on. Shouldn't my inner Shifus
have differing opinions?

196
00:11:30.909 --> 00:11:32.286
We are in total agreement...

197
00:11:32.286 --> 00:11:34.288
...with our mutual disappointment...

198
00:11:34.288 --> 00:11:35.455
...in you.

199
00:11:37.291 --> 00:11:38.292
Wait.

200
00:11:39.543 --> 00:11:42.963
He who resorts to violence now...

201
00:11:44.173 --> 00:11:47.509
will only find more violence later.

202
00:11:47.509 --> 00:11:48.468
Huh?

203
00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:54.016
So what you're saying is,
if we don't hurt Zhen a little now...

204
00:11:54.016 --> 00:11:55.976
We can hurt her a lot later.

205
00:11:55.976 --> 00:11:57.811
What? No, that's not what I said.

206
00:11:57.811 --> 00:12:01.857
Yes! And more violence later
is better than less violence now.

207
00:12:01.857 --> 00:12:04.234
No, no. I think you're misunderstanding
the fundamental point of--

208
00:12:04.234 --> 00:12:05.652
- More violence!
- Hooray!

209
00:12:05.652 --> 00:12:08.238
Violence makes my tummy tingle.

210
00:12:08.238 --> 00:12:10.365
You know, that panda
makes a lot of good points.

211
00:12:10.365 --> 00:12:13.994
- I like it.
- Violence, violence, violence.

212
00:12:13.994 --> 00:12:15.204
No, no, no! Wait!

213
00:12:15.204 --> 00:12:16.288
Come back!

214
00:12:16.288 --> 00:12:18.248
I'll come up with better wisdom.

215
00:12:19.041 --> 00:12:21.210
You have got to workshop
those proverbs.

216
00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.255
- Uh, the Kung Fu Panda?
- Nope.

217
00:12:25.255 --> 00:12:27.090
The son of Mr. Ping and Li?

218
00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:29.009
Those are both very common names.

219
00:12:29.009 --> 00:12:30.802
- Mentored by Oogway?
- Sorry.

220
00:12:30.802 --> 00:12:32.471
Trained by Master Shifu?

221
00:12:32.471 --> 00:12:34.681
- Oh! Master Shifu? Yes.
- Aha!

222
00:12:34.681 --> 00:12:37.142
Everyone's heard of
the legendary Master Shifu.

223
00:12:37.142 --> 00:12:38.185
But not you.

224
00:12:39.186 --> 00:12:41.647
Did someone say "legendary"?
Bring it in.

225
00:12:44.024 --> 00:12:45.025
Look, Han.

226
00:12:45.025 --> 00:12:48.028
I know we've had our differences,
but I'm really in a jam here,

227
00:12:48.028 --> 00:12:49.738
and I was hoping
you could help me out.

228
00:12:49.738 --> 00:12:51.573
- Thank you.
- Don't drink that.

229
00:12:53.534 --> 00:12:57.037
Oh!

230
00:12:57.037 --> 00:13:00.165
We just need someplace to lie low
for a while until the heat cools off.

231
00:13:00.165 --> 00:13:01.708
And why should I help you?

232
00:13:01.708 --> 00:13:04.378
Because deep down
beneath that iron-scaled exterior

233
00:13:04.378 --> 00:13:05.879
is a good-hearted soul

234
00:13:05.879 --> 00:13:07.798
who still thinks of me
as one of the family?

235
00:13:08.841 --> 00:13:09.967
Fine.

236
00:13:09.967 --> 00:13:13.512
But if you're still here by nightfall,
I'm calling the bulls myself.

237
00:13:14.221 --> 00:13:15.180
Sleep tight.

238
00:13:19.601 --> 00:13:21.520
So tonight, we take down The Chameleon.

239
00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.105
After you get your pants back.

240
00:13:23.981 --> 00:13:25.691
Not cool! You guys--

241
00:13:25.691 --> 00:13:27.317
Come on! Give them back.

242
00:13:27.317 --> 00:13:28.735
Those are custom.

243
00:13:35.075 --> 00:13:38.453
Yeah, this place doesn't
look very friendly.

244
00:13:39.288 --> 00:13:41.665
Oh! Oh, my tail.

245
00:13:42.583 --> 00:13:44.835
I'm sure everything is fine.

246
00:13:44.835 --> 00:13:46.295
This is a restaurant.

247
00:13:46.295 --> 00:13:49.298
These are my people.
We speak the same language.

248
00:13:49.298 --> 00:13:50.549
You wait here.

249
00:13:52.676 --> 00:13:54.428
Salutations!

250
00:13:54.428 --> 00:13:57.014
I'm so sorry to interrupt.

251
00:13:57.014 --> 00:13:58.473
I know you're having a good time,

252
00:13:58.473 --> 00:14:03.145
but I was wondering if a panda
happened to be passing by these parts?

253
00:14:03.729 --> 00:14:05.189
There was a panda here.

254
00:14:05.856 --> 00:14:06.940
You know him?

255
00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.735
Know him? Why, I'm his dad!

256
00:14:12.404 --> 00:14:14.031
No, no, no, no, no, no. Hmm?

257
00:14:14.656 --> 00:14:18.243
You need to pay
for what your son did to my tavern.

258
00:14:22.414 --> 00:14:25.542
My boy wouldn't have done this
for no reason.

259
00:14:25.542 --> 00:14:27.503
Is it possible your broth was bland?

260
00:14:27.503 --> 00:14:28.879
Try it.

261
00:14:29.379 --> 00:14:31.632
No, no!

262
00:14:31.632 --> 00:14:33.634
The broth smells excellent.

263
00:14:33.634 --> 00:14:37.387
You should not add a single thing,
especially not me!

264
00:14:37.387 --> 00:14:38.931
Hands off the goose.

265
00:14:42.601 --> 00:14:43.936
The panda's back.

266
00:14:43.936 --> 00:14:45.395
- He's back?
- He's back?

267
00:14:45.395 --> 00:14:46.480
No.

268
00:14:47.147 --> 00:14:50.234
But you're about to wish he was,

269
00:14:50.234 --> 00:14:52.694
'cause if you think he made a mess
of this place,

270
00:14:52.694 --> 00:14:55.656
you have no idea what I'm capable of.

271
00:14:55.656 --> 00:14:58.617
Everything he learned, he learned from me.

272
00:15:01.119 --> 00:15:02.830
Except one thing.

273
00:15:03.413 --> 00:15:04.373
Mercy.

274
00:15:05.582 --> 00:15:09.086
I don't know where he got that,
because I don't believe in it.

275
00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:13.924
Now, this can go one of two ways.

276
00:15:13.924 --> 00:15:18.303
The easy way,
in which you tell me where he is,

277
00:15:18.303 --> 00:15:19.388
or the hard way,

278
00:15:19.388 --> 00:15:22.140
in which you tell me where he is,

279
00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:24.101
but it's hard to understand
what you're saying

280
00:15:24.101 --> 00:15:25.477
because you have no teeth.

281
00:15:32.734 --> 00:15:34.152
Mah-jongg.

282
00:15:34.152 --> 00:15:37.239
I eat mah-jongg tiles for breakfast!

283
00:16:04.766 --> 00:16:05.976
Huh?

284
00:16:18.071 --> 00:16:19.072
Stay there!

285
00:16:19.072 --> 00:16:20.115
Where's our son?

286
00:16:20.115 --> 00:16:21.992
He took a boat to Juniper City.

287
00:16:21.992 --> 00:16:23.160
Which way?

288
00:16:24.369 --> 00:16:26.413
You know, a wise goose once--

289
00:16:26.413 --> 00:16:27.706
Time to go.

290
00:16:27.706 --> 00:16:29.041
Uh, yeah. Right.

291
00:16:59.655 --> 00:17:01.406
Okay, let's try this again.

292
00:17:01.406 --> 00:17:06.161
Stir the pot, roll the wok,
serve the dish, and ska-blam!

293
00:17:07.287 --> 00:17:09.998
Hey, where's the golden dragon
that's supposed to shoot out?

294
00:17:09.998 --> 00:17:11.834
Not gonna happen with a broom.

295
00:17:11.834 --> 00:17:13.001
Yeah? Still not bad though.

296
00:17:13.001 --> 00:17:18.340
Yeah. But stir later, roll higher,
and the word is "skadoosh."

297
00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:19.800
"Skadoosh" isn't a word.

298
00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.969
- And "ska-blam" is?

299
00:17:26.849 --> 00:17:27.933
Ska-blam!

300
00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:37.067
I gotta say, you're not
like any of the other masters I've met.

301
00:17:37.067 --> 00:17:39.194
Yeah, I know.
There's not a lot of pandas.

302
00:17:39.194 --> 00:17:42.114
No, you're, like, a good guy.

303
00:17:42.114 --> 00:17:44.533
Listen up. The coast is clear.

304
00:17:44.533 --> 00:17:46.994
Thieves, hit the streets.

305
00:17:46.994 --> 00:17:48.328
And you two,

306
00:17:48.328 --> 00:17:49.997
get out of my sight.

307
00:18:01.633 --> 00:18:02.801
Huh?

308
00:18:10.684 --> 00:18:13.604
I know I promised that I'd lead you
right to The Chameleon's front door,

309
00:18:13.604 --> 00:18:16.356
but the back door seems
a little more practical.

310
00:18:16.356 --> 00:18:20.694
I gotta say, Zhen,
you really are a fox of your word.

311
00:18:20.694 --> 00:18:22.821
A chewed-up peach pit?

312
00:18:22.821 --> 00:18:25.782
One from Master Oogway's peach tree
of heavenly wisdom.

313
00:18:26.909 --> 00:18:29.161
Eh, it's a Valley of Peace thing.

314
00:18:29.161 --> 00:18:33.415
It's supposed to remind me that every pit
holds the promise of a mighty tree.

315
00:18:35.667 --> 00:18:37.419
Maybe it'll do the same for you.

316
00:18:43.717 --> 00:18:45.010
Are you sure you wanna do this?

317
00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:47.888
As a wise Spiritual Leader once said,

318
00:18:47.888 --> 00:18:52.935
how may one kick butt,
if one doesn't seek a butt to kick?

319
00:18:55.312 --> 00:18:57.189
You're a real piece of work,
you know that?

320
00:18:57.189 --> 00:18:58.440
Thank you.

321
00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.068
Wait, was that a compliment or an insult?

322
00:19:01.068 --> 00:19:02.194
Yes.

323
00:19:10.828 --> 00:19:11.787
Whoa.

324
00:19:14.832 --> 00:19:16.375
Have you seen our son?

325
00:19:23.382 --> 00:19:24.508
- Sorry.
- Sorry.

326
00:19:24.508 --> 00:19:25.801
- Nope.
- Nah.

327
00:19:25.801 --> 00:19:27.761
Tell us you've seen our son.

328
00:19:30.389 --> 00:19:32.683
Wait, why are they leaving? You said yes.

329
00:19:33.517 --> 00:19:36.311
Hey, look. Po was here.

330
00:19:36.311 --> 00:19:38.772
Amazing, Li, but how can you tell?

331
00:19:38.772 --> 00:19:41.817
Oh, we pandas have a gift
for seeing what others cannot.

332
00:19:41.817 --> 00:19:44.236
Come on. There may be more clues up ahead.

333
00:20:19.062 --> 00:20:20.647
Why?

334
00:21:13.659 --> 00:21:14.993
That was close.

335
00:21:14.993 --> 00:21:16.370
- Look out!

336
00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.621
Huh?

337
00:21:19.665 --> 00:21:21.500
- Po!
- Stand back.

338
00:21:24.086 --> 00:21:25.629
- Whoa!

339
00:21:27.172 --> 00:21:29.591
- They're coming!
- Hurry! Help me lift the cage!

340
00:21:36.348 --> 00:21:37.432
It's no use.

341
00:21:37.432 --> 00:21:40.352
- We gotta brace it with something.
- Here, use my staff.

342
00:21:40.352 --> 00:21:42.521
All right, stand back. Here I go.

343
00:21:44.648 --> 00:21:45.691
Zhen?

344
00:21:47.734 --> 00:21:49.486
Where are you taking my staff?

345
00:21:51.363 --> 00:21:54.199
I think you mean my staff?

346
00:21:54.199 --> 00:21:58.036
You gave it to Zhen,
and now Zhen has given it to me.

347
00:21:58.036 --> 00:22:01.248
"Given to gain,"
I believe, is how it works?

348
00:22:01.248 --> 00:22:02.875
You were right, Zhen.

349
00:22:02.875 --> 00:22:04.293
He was an easy mark.

350
00:22:04.293 --> 00:22:05.669
Zhen...

351
00:22:05.669 --> 00:22:08.839
First rule of the streets:
Never trust anyone.

352
00:22:08.839 --> 00:22:10.841
I taught her that.

353
00:22:10.841 --> 00:22:13.552
And you thought my apprentice
was your friend?

354
00:22:13.552 --> 00:22:14.803
Apprentice?

355
00:22:14.803 --> 00:22:16.722
She's the one that took you in?

356
00:22:16.722 --> 00:22:19.141
Best thing that ever happened to her.

357
00:22:19.141 --> 00:22:22.519
You should have seen
the little guttersnipe before I found her.

358
00:22:22.519 --> 00:22:24.605
Mangy and half-starved,

359
00:22:26.023 --> 00:22:29.109
hanging out with those rejects
from the Den of Thieves.

360
00:22:50.589 --> 00:22:52.257
She had no fear.

361
00:22:53.592 --> 00:22:55.052
Such potential.

362
00:23:01.725 --> 00:23:03.352
So I took her in.

363
00:23:04.937 --> 00:23:07.231
I made her what she is today.

364
00:23:07.231 --> 00:23:08.815
Stand up straight.

365
00:23:08.815 --> 00:23:09.983
Yes, master.

366
00:23:09.983 --> 00:23:13.654
So you went through all of this just to
get me to give you the Staff of Wisdom?

367
00:23:13.654 --> 00:23:14.738
Why?

368
00:23:14.738 --> 00:23:20.619
I, too, came from humble beginnings
and dreamed of becoming something more.

369
00:23:21.161 --> 00:23:22.663
I wanted respect and power.

370
00:23:22.663 --> 00:23:25.415
I wanted to be a master of kung fu.

371
00:23:25.415 --> 00:23:26.500
Say what?

372
00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.087
I was turned away
from every training hall I went to.

373
00:23:30.087 --> 00:23:34.174
They would say I was too small, too lowly,

374
00:23:34.174 --> 00:23:37.386
and that kung fu was not my destiny.

375
00:23:37.386 --> 00:23:40.639
And so, I chose a different path.

376
00:23:40.639 --> 00:23:42.391
Sorcery.

377
00:23:42.391 --> 00:23:43.642
I grew.

378
00:23:44.601 --> 00:23:45.936
I excelled.

379
00:23:45.936 --> 00:23:49.773
And I got everything
I had ever dreamed of.

380
00:23:49.773 --> 00:23:52.734
- Everything except kung fu.

381
00:23:52.734 --> 00:23:56.947
Just because I can look like Tai Lung
doesn't mean I can fight like him.

382
00:23:58.073 --> 00:24:02.202
You see, Po, kung fu may be
performed by the body,

383
00:24:02.202 --> 00:24:05.289
but its secrets are housed in the spirit.

384
00:24:05.289 --> 00:24:07.916
And now that I have access
to the Spirit Realm--

385
00:24:07.916 --> 00:24:10.127
You're gonna steal Tai Lung's kung fu.

386
00:24:10.127 --> 00:24:13.714
His and those of every master villain
that came before me.

387
00:24:13.714 --> 00:24:18.635
And once I do, no one will dare
underestimate me again.

388
00:24:18.635 --> 00:24:20.679
You forgot about me.

389
00:24:23.432 --> 00:24:25.475
Don't bother, Po.

390
00:24:25.475 --> 00:24:30.647
Those bars are enchanted with
some very old and very powerful magic.

391
00:24:30.647 --> 00:24:34.610
You'd need at least ten Dragon Warriors
to get through them.

392
00:24:34.610 --> 00:24:36.153
Then I won't go through them.

393
00:24:36.153 --> 00:24:38.280
I'll go under them.

394
00:24:52.794 --> 00:24:55.214
Well, that's frustrating
for all sorts of reasons.

395
00:25:03.639 --> 00:25:04.973
Whoa!

396
00:25:32.543 --> 00:25:34.503
- Po!
- Zhen?

397
00:25:35.254 --> 00:25:36.630
My staff! Hand it over.

398
00:25:36.630 --> 00:25:39.633
I'm so sorry I lied to you.
I was just doing what I was told.

399
00:25:39.633 --> 00:25:41.969
Apologize later.
Right now, I have to stop The Chameleon.

400
00:25:41.969 --> 00:25:43.720
Po!

401
00:25:43.720 --> 00:25:45.055
Zhen?

402
00:25:50.185 --> 00:25:51.687
No!

403
00:25:57.776 --> 00:25:59.528
Well done, Zhen.

404
00:25:59.528 --> 00:26:01.738
You never said you were gonna hurt him.

405
00:26:01.738 --> 00:26:03.949
What's the second rule
of the streets?

406
00:26:04.908 --> 00:26:06.535
Someone always gets hurt.

407
00:26:06.535 --> 00:26:08.620
And make sure it's never you.

408
00:26:09.454 --> 00:26:12.416
I just wish there had been another way.

409
00:26:12.416 --> 00:26:14.126
Third rule of the streets?

410
00:26:14.626 --> 00:26:15.878
Third rule?

411
00:26:15.878 --> 00:26:18.505
Some would say
it's the most important:

412
00:26:18.505 --> 00:26:22.134
No one is interested in your feelings.

413
00:26:23.886 --> 00:26:26.388
Chop-chop!
We have a Spirit Realm to plunder.

414
00:26:27.472 --> 00:26:29.308
And smile.

415
00:26:29.308 --> 00:26:31.518
Nobody likes a grouch.

416
00:26:31.518 --> 00:26:35.147
Honestly, Zhen, I don't know where
you pick up such bad habits.

417
00:26:42.863 --> 00:26:43.864
If I could--

418
00:26:47.743 --> 00:26:48.702
Hey there.

419
00:26:49.495 --> 00:26:51.038
Whoa!

420
00:26:52.623 --> 00:26:55.083
Get off me! Ow! Ow!

421
00:27:00.297 --> 00:27:01.673
- Son!

422
00:27:09.473 --> 00:27:11.892
- Now save me.

423
00:27:13.227 --> 00:27:14.228
Hi, Son.

424
00:27:18.023 --> 00:27:20.651
It's okay. We've got you, Po.
We've got you.

425
00:27:23.028 --> 00:27:24.404
So you followed me.

426
00:27:24.404 --> 00:27:25.781
- It was his idea.

427
00:27:25.781 --> 00:27:27.741
Okay, okay. It was both our ideas.

428
00:27:27.741 --> 00:27:29.910
We only follow because we love.

429
00:27:29.910 --> 00:27:32.871
No, you followed
because you didn't believe in me.

430
00:27:34.081 --> 00:27:35.207
And because we love?

431
00:27:36.375 --> 00:27:38.377
Well, you're right.

432
00:27:39.002 --> 00:27:40.838
I screwed up big-time.

433
00:27:41.713 --> 00:27:43.549
I trusted the wrong person.

434
00:27:43.549 --> 00:27:46.134
I gave the Staff of Wisdom
right to The Chameleon.

435
00:27:47.803 --> 00:27:48.804
Oh...

436
00:27:49.513 --> 00:27:54.142
Po, that was a very big-time screw-up.

437
00:27:56.979 --> 00:28:00.524
If only I'd listened to Master Shifu
and stayed in the Valley of Peace,

438
00:28:00.524 --> 00:28:04.111
The Chameleon wouldn't have my staff,
and none of this would be happening.

439
00:28:04.111 --> 00:28:07.072
I was just so determined
to keep things the way they were.

440
00:28:07.072 --> 00:28:10.242
Everyone is afraid of change, Po.

441
00:28:10.242 --> 00:28:11.869
Even me.

442
00:28:11.869 --> 00:28:14.746
There was a time not so long ago

443
00:28:14.746 --> 00:28:19.668
when all I wanted to be was
the greatest noodle chef in the valley.

444
00:28:19.668 --> 00:28:21.128
So what happened?

445
00:28:21.712 --> 00:28:24.214
I became the greatest noodle chef
in the valley.

446
00:28:24.214 --> 00:28:25.340
It's true.

447
00:28:25.340 --> 00:28:27.384
But I also became a father.

448
00:28:28.093 --> 00:28:31.221
And nothing...
nothing's ever been the same since.

449
00:28:32.347 --> 00:28:34.683
Change doesn't always
have to be a bad thing.

450
00:28:34.683 --> 00:28:38.270
Why do you think I always change
the menu at the restaurant?

451
00:28:39.897 --> 00:28:42.441
Because if things stayed the same forever,

452
00:28:42.441 --> 00:28:45.319
sooner or later,
they would lose their flavor.

453
00:28:46.945 --> 00:28:48.071
He's right, Po.

454
00:28:48.071 --> 00:28:51.366
Since I left my village,
I've become a bit of a warrior.

455
00:28:51.366 --> 00:28:53.285
- Strong. Brave.

456
00:28:54.703 --> 00:28:56.538
- Move it.

457
00:28:56.538 --> 00:28:57.623
This way.

458
00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:00.959
Get those cages up there. Come on.

459
00:29:01.793 --> 00:29:03.879
Hmm. This looks bad.

460
00:29:03.879 --> 00:29:05.005
Really bad.

461
00:29:05.005 --> 00:29:06.089
Move it.

462
00:29:06.089 --> 00:29:08.008
- Come on.
